@api = https://dummyjson.com
@echo = https://httpbin.org

### Get a product
GET {{api}}/products/1
Accept: application/json

### Create a simulated product
POST {{api}}/products/add
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Lavender Notebook","price":120}

### Update a simulated product
PUT {{api}}/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Lavender Notebook Updated"}

### Delete a simulated product
DELETE {{api}}/products/1

### Query two users and select fields
GET {{api}}/users?limit=2&select=firstName,email

### Create a simulated post
POST {{api}}/posts/add
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Practical work 1","userId":1}

### Request headers without a response body
HEAD {{api}}/products

### Expected 404 response
GET {{echo}}/status/404

### Expected 500 response
GET {{echo}}/status/500

### Obtain a fresh public demo token
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"emilys","password":"emilyspass"}

### Authenticate with the token from the preceding request
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### List products; use curl -w for the timing measurements
GET {{api}}/products

### Inspect HTTPS; use curl -v for TLS diagnostics
GET {{api}}/products/1

### Inspect HTTP redirection; disable automatic redirects to see the original status
HEAD http://dummyjson.com/products/1

### Set demo cookies; use curl -c to inspect the Netscape jar
GET {{echo}}/cookies/set?user_role=student&session_key=lab1_token

### Echo the cookies; use curl -b for the jar lifecycle experiment
GET {{echo}}/cookies
Cookie: session_key=lab1_token; user_role=student

### Echo a Set-Cookie header with security attributes
GET {{echo}}/response-headers?Set-Cookie=session_id%3Dxyz789%3B%20Path%3D%2F%3B%20Secure%3B%20HttpOnly%3B%20SameSite%3DStrict

### Simulate a browser CORS preflight request
OPTIONS {{echo}}/post
Origin: https://my-college-app.edu
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type, Authorization
